1
00:00:05,530 --> 00:00:07,900
When I was a kid, some guy promised he'd go after me.

2
00:00:07,900 --> 00:00:08,900
Oh, you mean Aof.

3
00:00:08,900 --> 00:00:10,900
Seeing you join a club you're terrible at,

4
00:00:10,900 --> 00:00:12,500
I figured it out. Only one reason.

5
00:00:12,500 --> 00:00:15,500
I'm in upper secondary now, but Aof still hasn't made a move.

6
00:00:15,500 --> 00:00:17,970
The reason he hasn't made a move is that he's not single.

7
00:00:17,970 --> 00:00:20,670
I'm surprised you don't know football is a team sport.

8
00:00:20,670 --> 00:00:23,300
You're angry at what he said because it's true, Aof.

9
00:00:23,300 --> 00:00:24,470
Let me take you home.

10
00:00:24,470 --> 00:00:26,570
I really want to be with you today. Cheer me up.

11
00:00:26,570 --> 00:00:27,730
Check, please.

12
00:00:29,030 --> 00:00:31,530
The activity you've planned costs too much.

13
00:00:31,530 --> 00:00:33,830
If you won't change it, find the money to cover it.

14
00:00:33,830 --> 00:00:34,700
You said it.

15
00:00:34,700 --> 00:00:36,270
Because I will find a way.

16
00:00:36,270 --> 00:00:37,930
That kid Star is exactly like you, Din.

17
00:00:37,930 --> 00:00:39,500
Same way you argued with the seniors.

18
00:00:39,500 --> 00:00:41,130
Who should we push? / Star.

19
00:00:41,130 --> 00:00:43,970
But he has to show me he can really do it.

20
00:00:43,970 --> 00:00:45,770
I want to prove myself. That I can do it.

21
00:00:45,770 --> 00:00:47,630
I know the owner of the venue.

22
00:00:47,630 --> 00:00:51,400
Living this close to Fuen, I won't get lonely. And we can talk things over.

23
00:00:51,400 --> 00:00:53,330
I'll just step out to the restroom.

24
00:00:53,330 --> 00:00:54,330
What's with you today?

25
00:00:54,330 --> 00:00:56,270
I want to be around you today. Humor me?

26
00:00:58,600 --> 00:00:59,800
Hey, grab the ball.

27
00:01:02,670 --> 00:01:04,900
Even with you being my friend, I still can't do it.

28
00:01:04,900 --> 00:01:07,470
Fuen... that's the third one now.

29
00:01:07,470 --> 00:01:09,170
You still haven't figured it out?

30
00:03:23,030 --> 00:03:25,270
"Fuen, once you give Physics the present, tell me."

31
00:03:25,270 --> 00:03:26,530
"I wanna know if he's happy."

32
00:03:34,700 --> 00:03:36,270
Fuen.

33
00:03:46,000 --> 00:03:49,870
I thought it over, and if I give it to him myself,

34
00:03:49,870 --> 00:03:53,070
Physics will overthink it and won't dare take it.

35
00:03:54,200 --> 00:03:55,300
So...

36
00:03:55,300 --> 00:03:57,600
could you give it to Physics for me instead?

37
00:04:00,770 --> 00:04:02,630
Please, Fuen.

38
00:04:29,130 --> 00:04:30,300
You think it's nice?

39
00:04:31,400 --> 00:04:34,500
It's nice. Buy it.

40
00:05:09,730 --> 00:05:11,800
I don't know. Whatever happens, happens.

41
00:05:15,130 --> 00:05:17,470
Fuen, you haven't left for school yet?

42
00:05:17,470 --> 00:05:18,900
Waiting on Physics for a ride?

43
00:05:18,900 --> 00:05:21,170
He sleeps in. I can't be bothered waiting.

44
00:05:24,930 --> 00:05:26,570
Then how are you getting to school?

45
00:05:26,570 --> 00:05:28,430
Why not take the motorbike?

46
00:05:31,100 --> 00:05:33,070
Can't be bothered riding. The BTS is faster.

47
00:05:33,070 --> 00:05:34,900
I'm off, Mom. Bye.

48
00:05:35,670 --> 00:05:37,900
Then what did I buy you a motorbike for?

49
00:05:37,900 --> 00:05:39,530
Hmph. I heard that.

50
00:05:40,000 --> 00:05:40,800
Okay, sweetie.

51
00:05:40,800 --> 00:05:43,300
Travel safe, sweetie. Study hard.

52
00:06:27,370 --> 00:06:29,970
Why the world-on-your-shoulders face?

53
00:06:29,970 --> 00:06:32,570
Something wrong? Maybe I can help.

54
00:06:32,570 --> 00:06:34,500
It's heavier than the world.

55
00:06:35,770 --> 00:06:37,570
If I slip up even a little,

56
00:06:38,100 --> 00:06:40,200
you can start planning my funeral, Din.

57
00:06:41,600 --> 00:06:44,330
I'm screwed. I never should have taken it.

58
00:06:47,730 --> 00:06:49,130
It's about Physics, isn't it?

59
00:06:49,530 --> 00:06:50,830
How did you know?

60
00:06:51,770 --> 00:06:54,200
I didn't think I'd actually guess right.

61
00:06:54,200 --> 00:06:58,530
But the only thing that gets you like this is Physics.

62
00:07:10,070 --> 00:07:11,600
Thanks, Din.

63
00:07:25,370 --> 00:07:27,030
Morning, Mom.

64
00:07:28,100 --> 00:07:29,930
Oh, Physics, honey.

65
00:07:29,930 --> 00:07:32,670
Fuen just left for school.

66
00:07:32,670 --> 00:07:34,770
He went with Din. Didn't he tell you?

67
00:07:40,900 --> 00:07:44,530
He probably messaged me. I just haven't read it yet.

68
00:07:44,530 --> 00:07:47,400
It's all right, Mom. I'll head off now.

69
00:07:47,400 --> 00:07:48,870
Okay, honey. Okay, okay.

70
00:07:48,870 --> 00:07:51,300
Travel safe, honey. Study hard.

71
00:07:51,300 --> 00:07:52,270
Yes, ma'am.

72
00:08:10,730 --> 00:08:13,700
Fuen didn't come in with Physics.

73
00:08:17,270 --> 00:08:19,070
I'm so dead.

74
00:08:19,070 --> 00:08:20,500
Hey, don't die just yet, buddy.

75
00:08:20,500 --> 00:08:22,170
Wait till your daddy gets here first.

76
00:08:22,170 --> 00:08:23,700
Whoa.

77
00:08:25,370 --> 00:08:29,330
What am I supposed to do? He's gonna curse me out and beat me like an animal.

78
00:08:29,330 --> 00:08:32,200
The cursing part, you can relax. He'll curse you out for sure.

79
00:08:32,500 --> 00:08:33,770
Wow, that helps a lot.

80
00:08:33,770 --> 00:08:36,530
But I don't think he'll hit you. If you want my advice, though,

81
00:08:36,530 --> 00:08:38,600
maybe this time you try being cute.

82
00:08:38,799 --> 00:08:40,500
You think being cute is gonna save me?

83
00:08:40,500 --> 00:08:43,130
You don't remember? Back when he had it in for you.

84
00:08:43,130 --> 00:08:45,600
Like you'd stepped on his foot in every past life.

85
00:08:48,230 --> 00:08:51,030
Just try trusting Aof this once.

86
00:08:51,730 --> 00:08:54,000
Sweet-talk him a bit. He'll come around.

87
00:08:55,670 --> 00:08:58,370
Damn, you too?

88
00:08:59,000 --> 00:09:00,500
Damn it.

89
00:09:00,500 --> 00:09:02,900
Not one of you is any help.

90
00:09:05,270 --> 00:09:06,070
Really?

91
00:09:09,330 --> 00:09:10,900
It's not him, is it?

92
00:09:16,470 --> 00:09:19,300
You and I need to have a talk.

93
00:09:21,170 --> 00:09:22,670
Here's the thing, buddy.

94
00:09:29,830 --> 00:09:32,100
I'm sorry.

95
00:09:34,030 --> 00:09:35,400
I already feel bad about it.

96
00:09:36,400 --> 00:09:38,130
I couldn't sleep last night.

97
00:09:38,600 --> 00:09:42,100
And I left really early this morning.

98
00:09:42,100 --> 00:09:46,500
I didn't want to call and rush you awake or anything.

99
00:09:53,600 --> 00:09:57,000
So you came in with Din instead?

100
00:09:58,230 --> 00:10:03,400
No, no. I ran into him outside my house by chance.

101
00:10:03,400 --> 00:10:07,500
And he asked me to come along, that's all. It was nothing.

102
00:10:11,230 --> 00:10:12,630
You're easy, you know that?

103
00:10:14,230 --> 00:10:16,570
Anyone asks and off you go? Huh?

104
00:10:16,570 --> 00:10:20,770
Come on, it was just going to school together.

105
00:10:20,770 --> 00:10:21,870
And what about you?

106
00:10:21,870 --> 00:10:24,170
You go everywhere I ask, too.

107
00:10:26,530 --> 00:10:29,230
So, wanna come play games at my place tonight?

108
00:10:37,270 --> 00:10:38,530
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

109
00:10:40,230 --> 00:10:43,470
Just don't do it again. I don't like being left behind.

110
00:10:44,370 --> 00:10:47,900
Especially by you. Never again. Understand?

111
00:10:51,470 --> 00:10:52,700
Understood.

112
00:10:58,170 --> 00:10:59,200
Yes, yes, yes.

113
00:10:59,800 --> 00:11:03,530
You two act like this room is yours alone, walled off in your own world.

114
00:11:04,170 --> 00:11:07,000
Tang, can you even see me?

115
00:11:07,000 --> 00:11:09,630
Of course I can. Why can't they?

116
00:11:09,630 --> 00:11:14,830
Oh, Aof, my friend. You and I have plenty to talk about.

117
00:11:15,130 --> 00:11:18,430
Going out with my little brother — pretty fun, right?

118
00:11:23,970 --> 00:11:31,070
Oh, now I remember. I need to go train for our school's football team.

119
00:11:35,630 --> 00:11:37,670
You still won't accept Aof, will you?

120
00:11:40,130 --> 00:11:44,430
Look at him. Doing whatever he wants, day after day.

121
00:11:45,670 --> 00:11:47,370
I don't want to see Chemi get hurt.

122
00:11:51,500 --> 00:11:53,800
But I'd never hurt you, buddy.

123
00:11:58,800 --> 00:12:00,030
Go sit down for class.

124
00:12:01,500 --> 00:12:03,130
Is he even coming back to class?

125
00:12:27,370 --> 00:12:30,470
I'm thinking we throw a mini concert in the heart of Siam.

126
00:12:30,470 --> 00:12:34,230
And I'll ask FUN VIBE, our school band, to help out.

127
00:12:37,530 --> 00:12:39,970
The other day I helped them make some content,

128
00:12:39,970 --> 00:12:44,170
and after we posted the clip, the response was really good.

129
00:12:44,170 --> 00:12:46,170
Would you like to see?

130
00:12:56,430 --> 00:12:58,870
And the venue? Will they let us use it?

131
00:12:58,870 --> 00:13:00,630
Have you contacted them yet?

132
00:13:00,630 --> 00:13:01,930
I've already contacted them.

133
00:13:01,930 --> 00:13:04,200
They've given us permission to use this space,

134
00:13:04,200 --> 00:13:06,700
and they're giving us two hours, Din.

135
00:13:06,700 --> 00:13:08,370
Can you raise the money in that time?

136
00:13:08,400 --> 00:13:10,870
I'll need your help with the PR on this, Tonnam.

137
00:13:10,870 --> 00:13:16,570
But I've already come up with a hashtag — #ทฟวBusking.

138
00:13:17,630 --> 00:13:20,130
But with help from all of you seniors,

139
00:13:20,130 --> 00:13:22,530
I'm sure we can pull it off.

140
00:13:33,830 --> 00:13:35,730
We can help you with the PR,

141
00:13:37,770 --> 00:13:40,830
but everything else is still your responsibility.

142
00:13:40,830 --> 00:13:42,570
No problem at all, Din.

143
00:13:49,170 --> 00:13:51,000
Then could I have my phone back?

144
00:13:52,870 --> 00:13:57,370
Next is the music. I'd like to go talk to the band first.

145
00:14:00,570 --> 00:14:02,210
Is that all right, Din?

146
00:14:51,310 --> 00:14:53,570
I've got a favor to ask.

147
00:14:58,340 --> 00:15:02,240
We're putting on a busking show this weekend,

148
00:15:02,240 --> 00:15:05,510
so I wanted to invite FUN VIBE to play.

149
00:15:06,470 --> 00:15:08,470
Could you all help us out?

150
00:15:12,770 --> 00:15:16,870
If nothing comes up, of course we'd help, but...

151
00:15:18,070 --> 00:15:20,510
we've got a match that day. What time is it?

152
00:15:20,510 --> 00:15:24,010
We should finish around six. Think we'd make it?

153
00:15:24,010 --> 00:15:29,210
It's about an hour and a half from the match to Siam, if we hit traffic.

154
00:15:31,110 --> 00:15:33,370
It's not that we're busy.

155
00:15:33,370 --> 00:15:36,310
We're more worried about the instruments.

156
00:15:36,310 --> 00:15:40,340
The smaller instruments we can manage to carry,

157
00:15:40,340 --> 00:15:43,870
but the speakers and the drum kit would be tough.

158
00:15:43,870 --> 00:15:47,140
Then how about we have a drum kit ready for you?

159
00:15:47,570 --> 00:15:50,970
But there's still one more problem.

160
00:15:51,810 --> 00:15:52,970
Go on, tell him.

161
00:15:57,340 --> 00:16:00,410
I don't think I can stay till the end of your show, Star.

162
00:16:01,270 --> 00:16:04,140
I have to go abroad with my family.

163
00:16:04,140 --> 00:16:05,310
Huh?

164
00:16:07,610 --> 00:16:09,770
Can't you push your ticket back for him?

165
00:16:09,770 --> 00:16:11,510
It was booked ages ago.

166
00:16:14,170 --> 00:16:15,610
Sorry, Star.

167
00:16:18,240 --> 00:16:20,570
So we need to find another singer.

168
00:16:20,570 --> 00:16:23,710
It's all right. We'll look for a new singer.

169
00:16:24,510 --> 00:16:26,340
How about we hold auditions?

170
00:16:27,140 --> 00:16:29,140
That sounds like a plan. Let's do it.

171
00:16:29,140 --> 00:16:32,740
I'm telling you, the sign has to go right here.

172
00:16:32,740 --> 00:16:36,070
Nice and big. And right here, the speakers.

173
00:16:49,440 --> 00:16:51,510
Oops. / Hello.

174
00:16:51,510 --> 00:16:52,810
Uh, hello.

175
00:16:52,810 --> 00:16:54,140
First up, come on in.

176
00:16:55,370 --> 00:16:57,210
Hold on, hold on.

177
00:17:09,640 --> 00:17:11,609
The first one can come in now.

178
00:17:15,369 --> 00:17:16,240
Hello.

179
00:17:16,240 --> 00:17:17,510
What brings you here today?

180
00:17:17,510 --> 00:17:18,770
I'm here to sing.

181
00:17:18,770 --> 00:17:20,040
Go for it, then.

182
00:17:20,040 --> 00:17:21,069
Good luck.

183
00:17:22,210 --> 00:17:23,109
Thank you.

184
00:17:38,640 --> 00:17:40,170
Whoa-oh. / Oops.

185
00:17:40,170 --> 00:17:41,170
I'm sorry, what?

186
00:17:41,170 --> 00:17:42,740
Whoa-oh, sir.

187
00:17:42,740 --> 00:17:44,540
Whoa-oh what?

188
00:17:44,540 --> 00:17:46,940
Whoa-oh-oh. / Whoa-oh-oh. Oh.

189
00:17:48,140 --> 00:17:51,340
Okay, thank you very much. Thank you so much.

190
00:17:51,340 --> 00:17:52,540
Thank you.

191
00:17:52,540 --> 00:17:55,170
Send in the next one, please.

192
00:18:01,810 --> 00:18:04,140
Hello. / Hello.

193
00:18:04,140 --> 00:18:06,140
Please introduce yourself.

194
00:18:06,140 --> 00:18:09,140
Hello. I'm Ryuji, M.4/2.

195
00:18:10,310 --> 00:18:12,240
What brings you here today?

196
00:18:12,240 --> 00:18:14,270
I'm here to show you my dancing.

197
00:18:14,270 --> 00:18:16,540
But this is a singing audition.

198
00:18:16,540 --> 00:18:20,910
Um, well, I'll keep dancing and my vocal cords will kick in on their own.

199
00:18:23,310 --> 00:18:25,040
Go on, then. Hit it.

200
00:18:25,040 --> 00:18:27,440
Can I start? / Go for it.

201
00:18:50,770 --> 00:18:52,540
All out. / That really touched me.

202
00:18:53,270 --> 00:18:55,740
Can I go on and sing now?

203
00:18:55,740 --> 00:18:56,740
One moment, please.

204
00:18:57,140 --> 00:18:59,270
We've still got plenty of options.

205
00:18:59,270 --> 00:19:01,040
Maybe we should just sing it ourselves.

206
00:19:01,040 --> 00:19:02,270
Don't, Teu.

207
00:19:02,270 --> 00:19:04,770
I think you'd be worse than the first guy.

208
00:19:05,410 --> 00:19:08,910
I think that's enough for now, but thank you so much. Thank you.

209
00:19:08,910 --> 00:19:09,940
Thank you.

210
00:19:09,940 --> 00:19:13,010
Please keep Ryuji in your hearts.

211
00:19:13,010 --> 00:19:14,410
You got it.

212
00:19:14,410 --> 00:19:15,610
Thank you.

213
00:19:20,140 --> 00:19:21,340
This one looks promising.

214
00:19:22,310 --> 00:19:23,410
Hello.

215
00:19:25,710 --> 00:19:28,040
I'm here to sing and dance.

216
00:19:30,340 --> 00:19:31,540
Singing and dancing.

217
00:19:31,540 --> 00:19:33,840
A combo. / A combo. I like that.

218
00:19:35,340 --> 00:19:36,270
Looking good. / Okay.

219
00:19:36,270 --> 00:19:38,370
I say go for it. Hit it.

220
00:19:47,040 --> 00:19:51,510
Um, excuse me. I don't think singing and dancing together is working.

221
00:19:51,510 --> 00:19:52,970
Could I try just singing?

222
00:19:52,970 --> 00:19:54,810
Just singing? Sure, go ahead.

223
00:20:05,610 --> 00:20:08,310
You...

224
00:20:08,310 --> 00:20:10,210
I'm a big fan of yours, Star.

225
00:20:10,210 --> 00:20:12,410
Th-thank you.

226
00:20:13,070 --> 00:20:15,610
Anyway, thank you so much.

227
00:20:15,610 --> 00:20:19,340
You can head out now.

228
00:20:19,340 --> 00:20:20,970
Thank you so much.

229
00:20:20,970 --> 00:20:22,010
Good luck.

230
00:20:26,240 --> 00:20:29,240
Don't lose hope yet. Whoa-oh.

231
00:20:31,370 --> 00:20:32,310
Keep at it.

232
00:20:33,240 --> 00:20:34,410
Just a little more.

233
00:20:53,810 --> 00:20:57,070
Study up, man, or you're gonna fail.

234
00:20:57,340 --> 00:20:58,540
Whoa.

235
00:20:58,840 --> 00:21:00,570
I've got full marks in this one.

236
00:21:00,570 --> 00:21:01,970
Easy.

237
00:21:38,770 --> 00:21:44,170
♪ Maybe you'll never know there's someone waiting ♪

238
00:21:44,170 --> 00:21:50,710
♪ And every time, I'm still waiting — always waiting for you ♪

239
00:21:51,870 --> 00:21:58,410
♪ You're always here in my heart ♪

240
00:21:59,510 --> 00:22:04,610
♪ Maybe you were right when you said I'm too young ♪

241
00:22:04,610 --> 00:22:11,970
♪ But that's all right, I'll keep waiting until that day ♪

242
00:22:12,440 --> 00:22:18,140
♪ The day you're here with me ♪

243
00:22:21,670 --> 00:22:23,240
What are you all staring at?

244
00:22:23,240 --> 00:22:26,570
You're a living legend, my friend.

245
00:22:28,970 --> 00:22:31,970
You know what, you shouldn't have joined the football club.

246
00:22:31,970 --> 00:22:33,410
Music suits you way better.

247
00:22:33,410 --> 00:22:34,210
Right.

248
00:22:34,510 --> 00:22:36,540
I think there's still time to switch clubs.

249
00:22:36,870 --> 00:22:39,610
Our school's music club is full of talented people.

250
00:22:40,110 --> 00:22:41,510
You'd have more fun.

251
00:22:42,540 --> 00:22:44,370
I agree with them.

252
00:22:50,240 --> 00:22:55,540
♪ No matter how long it takes, my heart still calls for you ♪

253
00:22:55,540 --> 00:23:02,370
♪ Because this heart of mine is still waiting, only for you ♪

254
00:23:02,370 --> 00:23:06,410
♪ I want to tell you I love you ♪

255
00:23:06,410 --> 00:23:11,940
♪ Just like the first day we met ♪

256
00:23:11,940 --> 00:23:17,810
♪ Do you still think of me? Is it only me ♪

257
00:23:17,810 --> 00:23:22,040
♪ still waiting right here, going nowhere? ♪

258
00:24:02,340 --> 00:24:07,540
I can't take it. I can't handle this pressure.

259
00:24:07,540 --> 00:24:11,440
Ninety-nine percent of my life is already wrecked.

260
00:24:12,140 --> 00:24:15,670
Let me keep the last one percent for my parents to be proud of.

261
00:24:19,910 --> 00:24:22,370
Go on, study. Give that back.

262
00:24:23,470 --> 00:24:25,140
Work hard smart dog.

263
00:24:26,470 --> 00:24:29,470
Come on, let's go. Did you bring a pen?

264
00:24:31,370 --> 00:24:33,240
Oh, I forgot to bring a pen.

265
00:24:42,510 --> 00:24:45,840
Trust me, Star. Every problem has a way out.

266
00:24:46,240 --> 00:24:47,710
And what if there isn't one?

267
00:24:47,710 --> 00:24:50,010
You idiot, then go out the way you came in.

268
00:24:50,540 --> 00:24:54,570
True, but not everyone who can sing has to be in the school band, right?

269
00:24:54,570 --> 00:24:57,310
Really? But doesn't that already cover all the Rank S people?

270
00:24:57,310 --> 00:24:59,210
Or is there still a secret one out there?

271
00:25:00,140 --> 00:25:02,610
Ouch. You took him out with the very first shot.

272
00:25:04,570 --> 00:25:06,410
Stop pressuring me already.

273
00:25:07,070 --> 00:25:08,310
Sorry.

274
00:25:08,310 --> 00:25:09,810
Help me think.

275
00:25:12,370 --> 00:25:14,910
Star still hasn't found a singer?

276
00:25:15,740 --> 00:25:19,370
Probably not. Otherwise he wouldn't look this miserable.

277
00:25:20,670 --> 00:25:22,140
Can I go help him yet?

278
00:25:24,240 --> 00:25:25,740
There's no rush.

279
00:25:25,740 --> 00:25:27,470
If he can't find anyone,

280
00:25:28,770 --> 00:25:31,010
I'll be sending you two in myself.

281
00:25:34,070 --> 00:25:36,040
Come on, let's go eat.

282
00:25:42,470 --> 00:25:44,610
Or should we ask Phrues and Ply to help?

283
00:25:44,610 --> 00:25:47,470
They'd know people who've auditioned for the band.

284
00:25:47,470 --> 00:25:48,540
I'd feel bad.

285
00:25:49,610 --> 00:25:51,710
Everyone has already helped me so much.

286
00:25:53,410 --> 00:25:57,640
I don't want to give up, Time, but why is this so hard?

287
00:25:57,970 --> 00:25:59,410
Or ask Din to help.

288
00:26:00,070 --> 00:26:01,010
No way.

289
00:26:02,970 --> 00:26:07,740
If it means asking Din, I'd rather go ask...

290
00:26:10,710 --> 00:26:11,810
Hey.

291
00:26:11,810 --> 00:26:14,040
I know who can help us.

292
00:26:15,910 --> 00:26:17,270
Who?

293
00:26:21,010 --> 00:26:23,810
Let's go. / This is gonna be trouble.

294
00:26:36,140 --> 00:26:40,410
Who's he talking to? Watch where you're going.

295
00:26:40,710 --> 00:26:44,410
There he is, head down like he's about to burrow into the ground.

296
00:26:54,540 --> 00:26:57,240
Star's taking the school band busking in Siam,

297
00:26:57,240 --> 00:26:58,970
and he asked me to be their singer.

298
00:26:59,670 --> 00:27:02,640
Damn, that's the first time the kid's asked you for anything.

299
00:27:02,640 --> 00:27:07,110
But how did it get to you? Isn't their singer good?

300
00:27:07,110 --> 00:27:11,670
No idea, but I already said yes. I'm going to see him at his school this evening.

301
00:27:12,540 --> 00:27:15,870
Aren't you worried Mii will get hurt?

302
00:27:16,310 --> 00:27:18,870
I think if you're serious about Star,

303
00:27:18,870 --> 00:27:21,040
you need to sort things out with Mii first.

304
00:27:21,040 --> 00:27:24,910
Yeah, I'm with Nut on that. Saves you trouble later.

305
00:27:24,910 --> 00:27:29,340
I will. But let me be sure of my own feelings first.

306
00:27:31,140 --> 00:27:32,940
Shall we get something to eat?

307
00:27:32,940 --> 00:27:34,840
Yes. Let's go.

308
00:28:00,710 --> 00:28:02,610
All right, everyone. You may go home.

309
00:28:02,610 --> 00:28:05,010
Hand your work in to me tomorrow.

310
00:28:09,940 --> 00:28:14,040
Fuen, you're finishing it now? Not taking a break?

311
00:28:14,040 --> 00:28:16,640
Nah, I'm almost done.

312
00:28:19,570 --> 00:28:22,210
Hungry, then? I'll go buy you something.

313
00:28:22,210 --> 00:28:24,440
No need. We'll go together.

314
00:28:26,510 --> 00:28:27,470
Okay.

315
00:28:29,140 --> 00:28:31,470
You guys have got to help me.

316
00:28:31,470 --> 00:28:32,640
Look at this.

317
00:28:34,470 --> 00:28:39,170
My body is only on speaking terms with my feet. My hands are stiff as rocks.

318
00:28:39,170 --> 00:28:41,340
You swing that brush like it's a sword fight.

319
00:28:42,570 --> 00:28:44,440
Even in sword-fighting class,

320
00:28:44,440 --> 00:28:45,870
Hey, asshole, my work!

321
00:28:45,870 --> 00:28:47,610
you held the sword with your feet.

322
00:28:47,610 --> 00:28:49,240
You only use your hands to eat.

323
00:28:49,640 --> 00:28:52,140
Can't help it. When God made me,

324
00:28:52,140 --> 00:28:54,110
all he handed out was football skills.

325
00:28:54,840 --> 00:28:58,340
Fuen, you're the best in the class. Give me a hand.

326
00:29:00,570 --> 00:29:02,310
Done!

327
00:29:03,610 --> 00:29:05,670
Shit. / Aw, crap.

328
00:29:08,140 --> 00:29:11,410
Damn it, man. Were you even listening to me?

329
00:29:11,410 --> 00:29:15,340
So how far have you got? Let me see.

330
00:29:18,070 --> 00:29:22,510
Whoa, Aof. You'd better stick to kicking a ball.

331
00:29:22,810 --> 00:29:25,040
Oh, come on.

332
00:29:25,040 --> 00:29:26,870
It's fine. I'll help you.

333
00:29:27,970 --> 00:29:29,210
I'm counting on you, buddy.

334
00:29:41,570 --> 00:29:44,370
Hey, kid. Tuck your shirt in.

335
00:29:44,370 --> 00:29:47,410
Yeah, I'd better let the janitor know.

336
00:29:47,410 --> 00:29:49,170
The trash still isn't cleared.

337
00:30:01,470 --> 00:30:03,310
Hey, isn't that Rei?

338
00:30:03,310 --> 00:30:05,010
What's he doing at our school?

339
00:30:05,540 --> 00:30:08,410
So what now? Should we follow him?

340
00:30:08,410 --> 00:30:11,840
Nah, he wouldn't dare start anything at our school.

341
00:30:11,840 --> 00:30:14,610
Maybe he's got business with the football club.

342
00:30:14,610 --> 00:30:16,370
Yeah, could be.

343
00:30:17,040 --> 00:30:18,440
Let's get going.

344
00:30:24,640 --> 00:30:26,240
Whoa, Fuen.

345
00:30:28,040 --> 00:30:28,970
Shit.

346
00:30:28,970 --> 00:30:31,610
Hey, that's a bit much, Fuen.

347
00:30:31,610 --> 00:30:33,070
You bastard.

348
00:30:33,870 --> 00:30:36,540
I pay my respects, master. Will you take me as your disciple?

349
00:30:37,570 --> 00:30:38,840
Of course, young disciple.

350
00:30:38,840 --> 00:30:40,770
May I test my skills, master?

351
00:30:49,870 --> 00:30:50,710
Hmm.

352
00:30:53,510 --> 00:30:54,970
Physics, I'm sorry.

353
00:30:54,970 --> 00:30:57,070
I swear, my eyes were on the painting.

354
00:30:57,910 --> 00:30:59,670
All right. Okay, Aof, buddy.

355
00:31:00,310 --> 00:31:02,210
Now that's more like it.

356
00:31:06,170 --> 00:31:09,240
Buddy, I swear, I was aiming for your head.

357
00:31:09,240 --> 00:31:10,370
It got way more of you.

358
00:31:10,370 --> 00:31:11,340
Hey, what— / Ow!

359
00:32:25,270 --> 00:32:27,610
Having fun, are we? Fancy a water fight?

360
00:32:27,610 --> 00:32:29,670
Couldn't you wait for April, you brats?

361
00:32:29,670 --> 00:32:32,870
Think you're Van Gogh? Everything in your hands is art, is it?

362
00:32:32,870 --> 00:32:35,570
Including your teacher's face? Get a move on.

363
00:32:35,570 --> 00:32:37,670
Go get a water bucket and a mop right now.

364
00:32:37,670 --> 00:32:41,010
If this room isn't clean today, forget being artists.

365
00:32:41,010 --> 00:32:44,440
You'll stay on here as janitors. Still standing there? Move!

366
00:32:44,440 --> 00:32:46,070
Sorry, sir! / Sorry, sir.

367
00:32:47,240 --> 00:32:48,140
Oops. Sir.

368
00:32:48,140 --> 00:32:49,210
You got me dirty.

369
00:32:50,510 --> 00:32:51,410
Go!

370
00:32:51,910 --> 00:32:57,210
These kids. Think they're making a legend or something? Go make it at home.

371
00:33:01,740 --> 00:33:03,970
Where are you now?

372
00:33:22,410 --> 00:33:24,210
Oh, shit!

373
00:33:24,210 --> 00:33:25,870
Hey, Star.

374
00:33:25,870 --> 00:33:28,840
How did you get Rei here? If Din finds out, there'll be trouble.

375
00:33:30,370 --> 00:33:34,540
And what's he got to complain about? This is my event.

376
00:33:35,170 --> 00:33:36,640
I can bring in whoever I want.

377
00:33:36,640 --> 00:33:40,470
True, but Din just got in a fight with him at the cadet training center.

378
00:33:41,010 --> 00:33:43,010
I don't care. I've made my choice.

379
00:33:45,610 --> 00:33:48,810
Then let me introduce you to the rest of the band first.

380
00:33:51,240 --> 00:33:52,940
You two wait here.

381
00:34:05,470 --> 00:34:08,409
I think before we get a gig, we're gonna get trouble.

382
00:34:10,070 --> 00:34:11,810
Listen to me.

383
00:34:11,810 --> 00:34:14,139
Whatever you picture happening in your head,

384
00:34:14,139 --> 00:34:16,909
it's definitely gonna happen. Just watch.

385
00:34:16,909 --> 00:34:19,469
Then why the hell would you let it happen? / No idea.

386
00:34:19,840 --> 00:34:20,969
What are you two on about?

387
00:34:20,969 --> 00:34:21,770
Oh, shit!

388
00:34:23,139 --> 00:34:26,870
We came to watch you play. / Yes.

389
00:34:26,870 --> 00:34:28,469
After you. / After you.

390
00:34:31,810 --> 00:34:34,610
Go ahead. If you're ready, you can start.

391
00:34:49,110 --> 00:34:50,010
Hold on, hold on.

392
00:34:50,610 --> 00:34:53,409
Hope he bombs. / Hope he bombs.

393
00:34:53,670 --> 00:34:54,469
Praying now.

394
00:34:55,870 --> 00:34:58,110
Just play it the way you rehearsed,

395
00:34:58,110 --> 00:35:00,070
and I'll find my way in as we go.

396
00:35:00,740 --> 00:35:01,910
You can start whenever.

397
00:35:18,510 --> 00:35:21,870
Hold on. I don't think this is gonna work.

398
00:35:22,440 --> 00:35:25,370
I'll start us off, and you follow me.

399
00:35:25,370 --> 00:35:27,540
I'll count you in, okay?

400
00:35:28,570 --> 00:35:30,710
Three, two, one... go!

401
00:35:31,000 --> 00:35:34,280
♪ Just one look from you, straight at me ♪

402
00:35:35,320 --> 00:35:39,380
♪ and my heart already starts to melt ♪

403
00:35:39,380 --> 00:35:44,820
♪ The closer we get, the more my head spins, I can't breathe ♪

404
00:35:44,820 --> 00:35:47,900
♪ Restless, and I don't even notice ♪

405
00:35:48,480 --> 00:35:53,300
♪ Is this what they call having a crush? ♪

406
00:35:53,300 --> 00:35:57,680
♪ It happens every single time I see you ♪

407
00:35:58,400 --> 00:36:00,840
♪ Do you feel it the way I do? ♪

408
00:36:01,540 --> 00:36:05,700
♪ That burning, spinning feeling in your heart ♪

409
00:36:05,700 --> 00:36:10,080
♪ Does everything I do shake you at all? ♪

410
00:36:10,080 --> 00:36:16,460
♪ If you feel it too, I'd know my odds ♪

411
00:36:16,920 --> 00:36:19,880
♪ on the chance we fall in love ♪

412
00:36:21,410 --> 00:36:22,210
Solo!

413
00:36:47,840 --> 00:36:49,840
How was that, Star?

414
00:36:50,940 --> 00:36:52,510
It was great, Rei.

415
00:36:52,510 --> 00:36:53,910
Oh, crap!

416
00:37:01,210 --> 00:37:04,440
Come on, let's eat. My treat.

417
00:37:05,710 --> 00:37:07,070
Rei.

418
00:37:11,140 --> 00:37:13,570
It got really late today.

419
00:37:14,540 --> 00:37:17,710
Thank you, and thank your friends too.

420
00:37:18,370 --> 00:37:22,010
At first I didn't even think you'd actually come if I asked.

421
00:37:23,240 --> 00:37:25,870
And why did you think I wouldn't?

422
00:37:28,170 --> 00:37:30,870
Because it's got nothing to do with your school.

423
00:37:32,710 --> 00:37:34,410
It's true, it's nothing to do with me,

424
00:37:34,410 --> 00:37:36,040
but it has to do with you, Star.

425
00:37:37,210 --> 00:37:38,640
Next time, don't hesitate to ask.

426
00:37:45,540 --> 00:37:49,370
I had a lot of fun today. It's nice doing something new.

427
00:37:50,110 --> 00:37:54,740
And next time, if you really want to thank me, take me out for a meal.

428
00:38:04,610 --> 00:38:06,870
No need for pinky promises, Rei.

429
00:38:07,310 --> 00:38:08,470
It's a deal.

430
00:38:09,640 --> 00:38:10,910
Promise me.

431
00:38:12,040 --> 00:38:13,140
I promise.

432
00:38:17,410 --> 00:38:19,010
I'll head off, then.

433
00:38:19,740 --> 00:38:20,540
Let's go.

434
00:38:21,240 --> 00:38:22,510
Bye-bye.

435
00:38:50,340 --> 00:38:53,710
Hey... wanna play some games?

436
00:40:28,610 --> 00:40:31,410
Thank you. You can put it right here.

437
00:41:00,240 --> 00:41:05,110
2/10, not really into it. My friend's little brother got me into the scene.

438
00:41:05,110 --> 00:41:10,140
'Friend's little brother'? And he tagged me, too?

439
00:41:12,110 --> 00:41:14,310
Friend's little brother, my ass.

440
00:41:14,870 --> 00:41:18,240
If we're only brothers, then why say you want to be together?

441
00:41:19,270 --> 00:41:21,470
Aof, you jerk.

442
00:41:40,770 --> 00:41:45,370
So what are you buying me for my birthday this year?

443
00:41:48,640 --> 00:41:51,770
Tell me what you want and I'll buy it.

444
00:41:54,170 --> 00:41:58,010
Well... that Polaroid camera.

445
00:41:58,570 --> 00:42:00,940
The one I said was my baby.

446
00:42:07,910 --> 00:42:10,510
Pick something else. Isn't there anything else?

447
00:42:13,770 --> 00:42:14,970
Something else?

448
00:42:19,240 --> 00:42:20,770
A film camera, maybe.

449
00:42:37,170 --> 00:42:39,570
Thank you, Tongdao.

450
00:42:52,840 --> 00:42:54,270
Hello, Time.

451
00:42:54,270 --> 00:42:58,140
Did you ask Fuen yet? How did Physics like the present?

452
00:42:58,140 --> 00:43:02,340
Oh, I completely forgot. I've been busy with all sorts of things.

453
00:43:02,340 --> 00:43:04,010
I'll message Fuen right now.

454
00:43:04,010 --> 00:43:05,540
Okay.

455
00:43:11,010 --> 00:43:14,540
"Fuen, how did it go?"

456
00:43:18,870 --> 00:43:21,840
"I gave it to him."

457
00:43:21,840 --> 00:43:24,170
"He says thank you."

458
00:43:24,170 --> 00:43:27,710
"Thank you so much for helping me."

459
00:43:27,710 --> 00:43:31,240
"If there's anything you want, just say the word."

460
00:43:33,030 --> 00:43:35,110
"No need. I was glad to help."

461
00:43:35,110 --> 00:43:36,470
What are you typing?

462
00:43:36,470 --> 00:43:38,670
Come on, hurry up.

463
00:43:38,670 --> 00:43:40,070
Yeah.

464
00:44:24,600 --> 00:44:30,400
"Secret — thanks for remembering."

465
00:44:45,140 --> 00:44:46,570
What are you doing?

466
00:44:48,040 --> 00:44:50,710
Nothing. Just taking photos.

467
00:44:50,710 --> 00:44:52,070
Just messing around.

468
00:45:01,170 --> 00:45:04,310
All right, since we're already at it.

469
00:45:08,270 --> 00:45:10,040
Where's my present?

470
00:45:11,570 --> 00:45:13,710
What is it you want?

471
00:45:13,710 --> 00:45:15,310
Film has to wait till tomorrow.

472
00:45:15,810 --> 00:45:17,710
Come on. / Film shops are all closed.

473
00:45:17,710 --> 00:45:20,540
Fuen, you're a terrible actor.

474
00:45:20,540 --> 00:45:25,810
I can see the camera I want right there in that bag.

475
00:45:26,540 --> 00:45:27,810
Can I have it now?

476
00:45:32,940 --> 00:45:33,740
Uh...

477
00:45:34,970 --> 00:45:36,870
Or is it not mine?

478
00:45:37,070 --> 00:45:39,740
No, it's yours, but...

479
00:45:39,740 --> 00:45:43,340
Well then, thank you.

480
00:45:43,810 --> 00:45:47,910
Damn... I didn't think you'd actually buy it for me.

481
00:45:49,770 --> 00:45:51,410
Thanks, buddy.

482
00:45:51,410 --> 00:45:53,140
It's exactly what I wanted.

483
00:45:53,740 --> 00:45:55,440
Physics, but...

484
00:45:58,610 --> 00:46:00,170
Just like the reference.

485
00:46:00,570 --> 00:46:02,110
What does this say?

486
00:46:02,710 --> 00:46:05,010
Happy birthday...

487
00:46:06,310 --> 00:46:10,570
"HBD, Physics. — Star"

488
00:46:12,070 --> 00:46:13,370
Star.

489
00:46:21,210 --> 00:46:23,040
Why does it say Star?

490
00:46:25,540 --> 00:46:28,210
Fuen. Answer me.

491
00:46:29,640 --> 00:46:34,910
Star came to me for advice about your birthday present.

492
00:46:44,570 --> 00:46:46,540
So you told Star about my camera.

493
00:46:46,540 --> 00:46:51,270
Yes, but it's what you wanted anyway, and you were definitely going to buy it.

494
00:46:51,270 --> 00:46:52,070
Right.

495
00:46:53,970 --> 00:46:55,840
But I told only you about it.

496
00:46:56,410 --> 00:47:01,410
Which means I wanted it to be between the two of us.

497
00:47:03,970 --> 00:47:06,270
And you went and told someone else.

498
00:47:08,210 --> 00:47:09,310
How could you?

499
00:47:15,110 --> 00:47:17,970
I'm sorry. I didn't think you'd take it this seriously.

500
00:47:31,340 --> 00:47:34,770
Fuen, I could buy a camera like this myself.

501
00:47:34,770 --> 00:47:36,170
But the reason I told you

502
00:47:36,170 --> 00:47:37,840
is that I wanted it to come from you.

503
00:47:42,540 --> 00:47:44,210
Sometimes I just hoped that

504
00:47:45,040 --> 00:47:46,170
if it came from you,

505
00:47:47,740 --> 00:47:49,710
it would actually mean something to me.

506
00:48:09,210 --> 00:48:11,170
Give it back to him. I don't want it anymore.

507
00:48:14,940 --> 00:48:17,370
But he already bought it for you. / So what?

508
00:48:19,210 --> 00:48:22,310
Do I have to accept whatever anyone buys me? Huh?

509
00:48:23,440 --> 00:48:24,640
Physics.

510
00:48:26,470 --> 00:48:29,410
Does this have to be such a big deal?

511
00:48:31,770 --> 00:48:32,910
Yeah.

512
00:48:34,610 --> 00:48:36,440
It is a big deal to me.

513
00:48:39,140 --> 00:48:41,310
But I guess you wouldn't understand.

514
00:48:43,110 --> 00:48:46,070
In the end you still think I'm being ridiculous.

515
00:48:58,110 --> 00:49:00,170
You don't understand me at all.

516
00:49:03,970 --> 00:49:06,470
Physics. Physics.

517
00:49:07,710 --> 00:49:08,570
Physics.

518
00:49:10,010 --> 00:49:10,870
Physics.

519
00:49:11,170 --> 00:49:12,610
Physics, where are you going?

520
00:49:13,110 --> 00:49:15,240
Hey, let's talk about this.

521
00:49:15,940 --> 00:49:17,610
Physics!

522
00:49:28,670 --> 00:49:30,140
What do you want?

523
00:49:31,970 --> 00:49:33,640
I'm sorry.

524
00:49:34,710 --> 00:49:36,270
Sorry about what?

525
00:49:36,610 --> 00:49:38,740
I'm sorry I hurt you.

526
00:49:44,210 --> 00:49:48,770
What hurts me is that my feelings

527
00:49:50,340 --> 00:49:52,610
are such a small thing to you.

528
00:50:43,270 --> 00:50:52,470
♪ I can't find the answer ♪

529
00:50:53,610 --> 00:50:58,770
♪ If I'd known this was all the road we had ♪

530
00:50:58,770 --> 00:51:03,940
♪ I'd have spent that time making it count ♪

531
00:51:03,940 --> 00:51:10,370
♪ But in the end the story stops right here ♪

532
00:51:10,370 --> 00:51:15,210
♪ We'll never get to love each other again ♪

533
00:51:25,910 --> 00:51:39,240
♪ And in the end the story stops right here — you and I were never meant to be ♪

534
00:51:42,840 --> 00:51:47,290
"From now on, this is a secret between us."

535
00:51:47,940 --> 00:51:52,770
"Look, guys. That's the little brother of my best friend from high school."

536
00:51:53,600 --> 00:51:58,400
"Don't you think Rei's been quiet lately about picking on our students?"

537
00:51:59,120 --> 00:52:03,970
"Isn't it better with no trouble? Besides, we're in M.6. Time to focus on our own lives."

538
00:52:04,370 --> 00:52:05,730
You had a fight with Fuen, huh?

539
00:52:05,730 --> 00:52:09,100
I'm running out of patience with you, so do me a favor and stay away.

540
00:52:09,100 --> 00:52:10,400
You don't want me around, huh?

541
00:52:10,400 --> 00:52:12,170
Let's not talk right now, you and I.

542
00:52:12,170 --> 00:52:13,470
I know you want me to dump Rei.

543
00:52:13,470 --> 00:52:14,870
But right now I really can't.

544
00:52:14,870 --> 00:52:16,670
Do you know who Rei's chasing these days?

545
00:52:16,670 --> 00:52:18,300
He's hitting on everyone.

546
00:52:18,300 --> 00:52:21,330
Nothing against you, but what you did to my friend was fucked up.

547
00:52:21,330 --> 00:52:22,770
Who? Din?

548
00:52:22,770 --> 00:52:25,000
Change the singer. I'm asking you.

549
00:52:25,000 --> 00:52:27,170
If that's your only reason, I don't see the point.

550
00:52:27,170 --> 00:52:29,170
I can't sing for you this evening, Star.

551
00:52:29,170 --> 00:52:30,730
Who sings in Rei's place then?
